From a41a0ae75538f464ba7855059e6a2f5c135bf774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:30:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/19] chat template: cache autoparser analysis, PEG parser
 and generation prompt [w6-6 a4-s2]

common_chat_templates_apply_jinja recomputed three things per request that
only depend on the template and the non-message inputs: the differential
autoparser analysis, the PEG parser + grammar generation, and the
generation-prompt diff (two extra full template renders). Measured floor:
6.8 ms/request even at 2 messages, ~70 ms @400 messages.

Three caches inside common_chat_templates (per instance, mutex-protected,
LLAMA_CHAT_TEMPLATE_CACHE=0 to disable):
- analysis: autoparser::analyze_template memoized per template object (pure
  function of the template source)
- generation prompt: keyed on template + bos/eos + enable_thinking + tools +
  add_bos/add_eos (every non-message input of the two diff renders); the
  cached value is verified against the fresh render (the formatted prompt
  must end with it) and re-resolved under cold-path conditions (extra_context
  cleared, matching the original compute order) - a genuine mismatch updates
  the entry and rebuilds the parser; specialized templates bypass the cache
  (their gen prompt is not verifiable on this path)
- parser: keyed on template + generation prompt + tools/tool_choice/
  json_schema/parallel_tool_calls/reasoning_format (messages are never used
  by peg_generator); prompt and generation_prompt are always recomputed

With LLAMA_CHAT_TEMPLATE_CACHE=0 all three mechanisms stay off and the
analysis runs per call like the original path, including the always-on
arena.load (review R1: the env switch now reproduces the pre-card behavior
exactly).

The arena.load used only by a LOG_DBG line is otherwise evaluated only when
debug verbosity is on (it re-parses the whole grammar string every request).

Review R5: removed the unused entry::size_bytes() dead code from the S1
token-prefix cache (memory cap stays by LRU count of 4 entries).

tests/test-chat-template-cache.cpp: formatted-text differential across all 62
templates in models/templates (grow / mid-prefix edit / tools on-off /
tool_choice / agp+thinking flags / kwargs / json_schema): cold vs warm apply
byte-identical (3720 applies, 0 failures). ChatML measure @300 KB: 195 -> 48
ms (4.0x). Regression evidence post-R1: logs/wave6/w6a4-regression.log.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai
